<title>NETHERLANDS: DUTCH SHELL CUTS DIESEL PRICES BY ONE CENT.</title>
<headline>DUTCH SHELL CUTS DIESEL PRICES BY ONE CENT.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Royal Dutch/Shell unit Shell Nederland BV said on Thursday it will cut its retail price for diesel in the Netherlands by one cent per litre with effect from March 1.</p>
<p>The move reflects changes in international product prices and the value of the dollar against the guilder, the company said.</p>
<p>From Saturday, the recommended price of diesel at Shell's self-service stations falls to 1.454 guilders per litre.</p>
<p>The price of premium with lead substitute will remain unchanged at 2.17 guilders, that of Euro regular unleaded at 2.05 guilders and that of premium leaded at 2.10 guilders.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000</p>
</text>
